abstract: |
  rnull-framework implements Causal Transparency Algebra (ℝ∅): the real numbers extended with one element, ∅ ("no value was supplied"), which is distinct from a measured zero and acts as the identity of both addition and multiplication.

  This release contains:
  - a NumPy reference implementation of the algebra, linear layers and optimisers;
  - an equivalent, optional PyTorch implementation, with layers that skip missing inputs, report their coverage and abstain when all inputs are missing;
  - exact freezing of selected parameter entries;
  - a Verilog multiply-accumulate cell with a 1-bit null tag per operand, self-checking testbenches and a bit-accurate Python model;
  - reproducible benchmarks with stored results, and a technical note with definitions and proofs.

  Status: research prototype. In the included experiments the null-aware layers show no accuracy advantage over imputation, and the hardware cell has not been synthesised. See CHANGELOG.md for the claims of v1.0.1 that later versions correct or withdraw.
